meta {
  name: Wait for generation
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assessments/{{assessmentId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

script:pre-request {
  // Generation is batched LLM calls plus validation plus an embedding pass for dedupe.
  // On CPU-only Ollama that is roughly a minute; on a hosted provider, seconds.
  await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 75000));
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

tests {
  test("finished, and not with an error", function () {
    const paper = res.getBody();
    expect(paper.status, paper.error || "no error reported").to.not.equal("generating");
    expect(paper.status).to.equal("draft");
  });
}

docs {
  A deliberate 75-second wait, because generation is genuinely slow on CPU. If your model
  is faster, shorten the pre-request script; if it times out, re-run this request until
  `status` leaves `generating`.

  **Fewer questions than you asked for is correct, not a failure.** The prompt says to
  return fewer rather than invent one the passage cannot support, and every question is
  then validated (self-referential stem, duplicate options, invented provenance) and
  deduped by stem embedding. A thin source legitimately yields two questions out of four.

  A terminal failure writes a sentence into `error` that is fit to show the author.
}
